{"version":"1","id":"apollo","handle":"apollo","name":"Apollo Blog","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/cb3bc4fd879a485cacd1cff99536c010","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-5.2827,"y":-2.4121,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":183,"newest_post_at":"2023-12-20T16:02:32.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2020-09-01T20:17:18.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.021858,"listicle_ratio":0.032787,"question_ratio":0.016393,"avg_read_time":4.823529,"summary_length_avg":306.977401,"title_length_avg":50.442623,"title_length_var":300.345069,"tag_entropy":2.950724,"tag_diversity":0.47541,"top_tag_share":0.382514,"avg_upvotes":0.846995,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.038251,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.051282,"zero_engagement_share":0.650273,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":1.06243,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.063953},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-4.1471,2.1912],"cadence_depth":[2.5882,-2.8235],"hype_variety":[5.25,-2.7353],"title_style":[-0.1324,7.0588]},"top_tags":[["graphql",170],["apollo",80],["general-programming",17],["community",15],["security",14],["discord",11],["react",11],["kotlin",11]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Announcing Apollo Router v1.0","Why use GraphQL?","Apollo Studio: A GraphQL IDE for every environment"],"outlier":["<strong>Apollo Federation and GraphOS add support for entity interfaces to streamline collaboration</strong>"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"n6FL89Zpk","title":"Apollo 3.9 Beta Feature Spotlight \u2013 The memory story","url":"https://www.apollographql.com/blog/apollo-3-9-beta-feature-spotlight-the-memory-story","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/apollo-3-9-beta-feature-spotlight-the-memory-story-n6fl89zpk","summary":"Apollo Client 3.9 Beta fixes memory leaks, adds granular control over internal cache sizes, and deprecates the canonizeResults option.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4921cb34d465328e165225c13d74ef92?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-20T16:02:32.000Z"},{"id":"y6TYxLIxf","title":"Centrally enforce policy as code for GraphQL APIs","url":"https://www.apollographql.com/blog/centrally-enforce-policy-as-code-for-graphql-apis/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/centrally-enforce-policy-as-code-for-graphql-apis-y6tyxlixf","summary":"GraphQL can be used as a central orchestration layer to accelerate development velocity for frontend and backend teams. GraphOS provides GraphQL-native workflows for implementing access control declaratively. Directives such as @authenticated, @requiresScopes, and @policy can be used to enforce authorization policies in the GraphOS router.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d6a801313ed0f82e0a67d250616655d2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-12T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"2W0bGljyg","title":"Apollo Client Office Hours with Alessia Bellisario","url":"https://www.apollographql.com/blog/apollo-client-office-hours-with-alessia-bellisario/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/apollo-client-office-hours-with-alessia-bellisario-2w0bgljyg","summary":"Alessia Bellisario and Jeff Auriemma discuss Apollo Client, including its release process, federated subscription support, and the defer and nonreactive directives. They also talk about upcoming public speaking engagements and testing improvements in Apollo Client.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8a4c86e1de722b4b73b6d2ba920e6acb?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-08T17:46:38.000Z"},{"id":"0EMMiDh9N","title":"Deploying the Apollo Router at Apollo","url":"https://www.apollographql.com/blog/deploying-the-apollo-router-at-apollo/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/deploying-the-apollo-router-at-apollo-0emmidh9n","summary":"Apollo recently upgraded to the Apollo Router with positive results in terms of performance, resource consumption, and scalability. Migrating from the Gateway to the Router required mapping custom functionality. The Router provides a standard execution environment and is simpler to deploy compared to a custom Gateway.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8a4c86e1de722b4b73b6d2ba920e6acb?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-06T12:32:40.000Z"},{"id":"RN5vJYlCq","title":"New GraphQL observability and insights in GraphOS Studio","url":"https://www.apollographql.com/blog/new-graphql-observability-and-insights-in-graphos-studio/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-graphql-observability-and-insights-in-graphos-studio-rn5vjylcq","summary":"Apollo has released a new and improved insights dashboard in GraphOS Studio for API owners operating a supergraph. The dashboard provides scalable observability tools and features a consolidated and streamlined experience, fast search capabilities, and improved list load times.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8f78409f06efe50c959dc9b4716aef74?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-31T16:11:06.000Z"},{"id":"9KEFKr8kz","title":"Announcing official Apollo Federation support for .NET with Hot Chocolate and Federation 2!","url":"https://www.apollographql.com/blog/announcing-official-apollo-federation-support-for-net-with-hot-chocolate-and-federation-2/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/announcing-official-apollo-federation-support-for-net-with-hot-chocolate-and-federation-2--9kefkr8kz","summary":"Apollo Federation has announced official support for .NET with a new library for Hot Chocolate. This library adds Federation support to Hot Chocolate's GraphQL server and includes features such as field migrations and flexible type ownership. The .NET community has been creating subgraphs using GraphQL .NET and Hot Chocolate, and this official support aims to better support their needs. Upgrading existing Hot Chocolate subgraphs to Federation 2 is also possible. Apollo plans to continue maintaining and improving the official Federation support for Hot Chocolate.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/99d2235238ea46c9cf83e5795bcac73e?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-24T15:46:07.000Z"},{"id":"FFYO3ngzm","title":"GraphOS Persisted Queries are generally available","url":"https://www.apollographql.com/blog/graphos-persisted-queries-are-generally-available/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/graphos-persisted-queries-are-generally-available-ffyo3ngzm","summary":"GraphOS Persisted Queries is a scalable solution for mitigating the risks of unbounded operations in GraphQL supergraphs. It enables platform teams to centrally register trusted GraphQL operations and safelist them, enhancing API security.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/2d6f94124e72957eb8284e95fe622523?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-11T17:18:15.000Z"},{"id":"4o6uIsOiy","title":"Apollo\u2019s Response to CVE-2023-38545","url":"https://www.apollographql.com/blog/apollos-response-to-cve-2023-38545/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/apollo-s-response-to-cve-2023-38545-4o6uisoiy","summary":"A high-severity vulnerability (CVE-2023-38545) has been found in curl and libcurl. Details will be disclosed on October 11. Apollo has reviewed their projects and found no usage of curl in most of them.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9a4212570827bdd524e3694237769810?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-09T14:59:26.000Z"},{"id":"jbdOhU4XK","title":"Leveraging GraphQL for Next-Generation API Platforms","url":"https://www.apollographql.com/blog/leveraging-graphql-for-next-generation-api-platforms/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/leveraging-graphql-for-next-generation-api-platforms-jbdohu4xk","summary":"The article discusses the importance of APIs in modernization initiatives and how REST and GraphQL can be used in a complementary manner. It highlights the joint efforts of Kong and Apollo in creating a unified reference architecture for building and operating a modern API platform.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/87219c3595b72fc32759d787edf0794e?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-06T12:20:25.000Z"},{"id":"ei6EYGhOy","title":"Enforcing GraphQL security best practices with GraphOS","url":"https://www.apollographql.com/blog/enforcing-graphql-security-best-practices-with-graphos/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/enforcing-graphql-security-best-practices-with-graphos-ei6eyghoy","summary":"Learn how GraphOS can help secure GraphQL APIs by centralizing authorization, safelisting registered operations, and limiting operation complexity. Discover security best practices at GraphQL Summit.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/bab2121f736ae30f88a4d0a1a2e7ba46?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-05T14:44:53.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["haskellwkly","ruby","solidity","smallstep","javaworld"],"opposite_handles":["alexfinn","tbpn","ryolu_","kloss_xyz","felixrieseberg"],"similar":[{"id":"haskellwkly","handle":"haskellwkly","name":"Haskell Weekly","is_squad":false,"x":-5.0636,"y":-2.643,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":251,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/e30aaf87f5af479cab08b891bb4fcaaa","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.980478,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":3.294821,"tag_diversity":0.278884},"top_tags_preview":[["haskell",250],["functional-programming",141],["general-programming",38]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-7.8824,-6.5147],"cadence_depth":[4.0294,-6.1324],"hype_variety":[